igest":"b7f0151399ee7c4377d90ed1d4bb6c977efcb82528bbccfc245e32069aa55163","schemaVersion":2,"submitted":{"artifactPath":"/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc/.insrc/artifacts/LLD-470a1f61b26b12c6-s1.json","attempt":1},"attempts":[{"number":1,"status":"incomplete","preparationKind":"planning","baseline":{"subjectFingerprints":{"canonical":"b04bc9da3e114d1b415cdeb244fa685ca2c2e4f73623e64db3801d8f03a2b41a","document":"a5c4e73cbb5de170a611941089ef261f3c0a105e8eec2b7f37d373f41a808f96"},"contentIdentity":"d95342d6c6e808eac8f83e31635891c599d693bdacff2ee90cba85baaa55c9eb","reviewedContent":{"canonical":"{\n  \"meta\": {\n    \"workflow\": \"design.story\",\n    \"runId\": \"wf-1794738660757-dh2adn\",\n    \"repoPath\": \"/home/subho/work/dev/insors/insrc\",\n    \"createdAt\": \"2026-11-15T10:36:58.303Z\",\n    \"epicCreatedAt\": \"2026-11-14T08:55:28.320Z\",\n    \"attribution\": {\n      \"outputs\": [\n        {\n          \"role\": \"(client)\",\n          \"tier\": \"core\",\n          \"runner\": \"cli-codex\",\n          \"model\": \"unknown\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    \"elapsedMs\": 352716,\n    \"repoIndexedAt\": null,\n    \"schemaVersion\": 1,\n    \"epicHash\": \"470a1f61b26b12c6\",\n    \"epicSlug\": \"rework-review-preparation-context-lifecycle-end\",\n    \"storyId\": \"s1\",\n    \"hldBaseRunId\": \"wf-1794738660757-dh2adn\",\n    \"hldEffectiveHash\": \"c990be2b3102c4689ac10509c7511de8fa68638f5b91f1d164c5a2fe23486811\",\n    \"hldAmendmentsApplied\": [],\n    \"storyTitle\": \"Rework review preparation and context lifecycle end to end\",\n    \"standalone\": true,\n    \"sizeClass\": \"bugfix\",\n    \"authoredBy\": \"controller\",\n    \"lifecycle\": {\n      \"status\": \"draft\",\n      \"revision\": {\n        \"number\": 4,\n        \"contentHash\": \"e8ef19d741844acdad653a2960d7a19660bbd2e056e103353cac2692ce2698c6\",\n        \"at\": \"2026-11-15T10:37:00.330Z\",\n        \"by\": {\n          \"id\": \"insrc:system\",\n          \"kind\": \"system\",\n          \"properties\": {}\n        }\n      },\n      \"signoffs\": []\n    },\n    \"envelope\": {\n      \"attachments\": []\n    },\n    \"revision\": 4\n  },\n  \"body\": {\n    \"summary\": {\n      \"audience\": \"technical\",\n      \"prose\": \"Preparation becomes one lifecycle-wide responsibility for both code and design review. Complete qualified context is reused under a private daemon-owned generation, while author, workflow and artifact freshness remain independently checked. Pinned input/feedback history stays in the review checkpoint; bounded live process/progress state moves out of the large history file, removing per-command rewrite amplification. Cold recovery, cancellation and publication use the same authority and durability rules as normal execution. The T14 revision makes prepared views bounded during construction and every lifecycle read: complete packets and history are staged as immutable descriptors and leaves rather than retained or decoded together. The existing memory/disk limits and full-workload release gates remain unchanged.\"\n    },\n    \"hldContextSlice\": {\n      \"frameworkSummary\": \"Standalone feature — no parent HLD. Design directly against the repo, grounded on the s1 analyze passes. There are no HLD shared contracts to honour.\",\n      \"ownedContracts\": [],\n      \"consumedContracts\": [],\n      \"boundary\": {\n        \"storyId\": \"s1\",\n        \"owns\": [],\n        \"depends\": [],\n        \"internal\": \"Rework review preparation and context lifecycle end to end\"\n      },\n      \"adjacentBoundaries\": [],\n      \"rolloutPhase\": \"standalone\",\n      \"nonFunctional\": {}\n    },\n    \"contractDetails\": {\n      \"surfaceLevel\": \"internal-shared\",\n      \"api\": [\n        {\n          \"name\": \"prepareReviewAdmission\",\n          \"signature\": \"prepareReviewAdmission(project: string, reviewId: string, attempt: number, input: unknown, reviewer: ReviewerParty, sources: ReviewSources, context?: ReviewAdmissionContext): Promise<AdmittedReview>\",\n          \"parameters\": [\n            {\n              \"name\": \"project\",\n              \"type\": \"string\",\n              \"purpose\": \"Canonical registered project\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"name\": \"reviewId\",\n              \"type\": \"string\",\n              \"purpose\": \"Existing exact review identity\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"name\": \"attempt\",\n              \"type\": \"number\",\n              \"purpose\": \"Pinned sequential attempt\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"name\": \"input\",\n              \"type\": \"unknown\",\n              \"purpose\": \"Complete submitted packet or pinned resume input\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"name\": \"reviewer\",\n              \"type\": \"ReviewerParty\",\n              \"purpose\": \"Host-resolved independent party\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"name\": \"sources\",\n              \"type\": \"ReviewSources\",\n              \"purpose\": \"Session-scoped verified/batched source interface\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"name\": \"context\",\n              \"type\": \"ReviewAdmissionContext\",\n              \"purpose\": \"Existing route/recovery context plus private preparation-session capability\",\n              \"optional\": true\n            }\n          ],\n          \"returns\": {\n            \"type\": \"Promise<AdmittedReview>\",\n            \"meaning\": \"Complete qualified admission and a private context binding; no selected task inventory before qualification.\"\n          },\n          \"errors\": [\n            {\n              \"type\": \"TaskReviewInputError\",\n              \"condition\": \"Typed family input/context validation rejects identity, scope, capability, capacity or freshness; unknown wire input is intentional and must pass exact decoding.\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"type\": \"CheckpointSaveError | Error\",\n              \"condition\": \"Existing code atomic writer reports a definitive/uncertain save outcome; design/host/native adapters preserve their concrete Error subclasses and pointed reason, never convert unavailable proof into success.\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"preconditions\": [\n            \"The approved issue is the implementation scope; existing source, route, history, attribution and capacity checks remain mandatory.\",\n            \"The host owns the exact review/attempt and has durably acknowledged input plus runtime initialization.\"\n          ],\n          \"postconditions\": [\n            \"One preparation session covers historical and current source requests; each immutable query is physically fetched once per session unless a bounded retry is explicitly recorded.\",\n            \"Already qualified immutable generations may be consumed through a current host receipt; mutable author/route/BUILD/permanent-history checks run anew.\",\n            \"No native work or reviewer invocation is authorized by a disk manifest alone.\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"prepareReviewPacket\",\n          \"signature\": \"prepareReviewPacket(input: unknown, sources: ReviewSources, historical?: boolean, route?: StoryRoute, stored?: StoredDerived): Promise<PreparedReviewPacket>\",\n          \"parameters\": [\n            {\n              \"name\": \"input\",\n              \"type\": \"unknown\",\n              \"purpose\": \"Exact packet; selected after-segments/deletion anchors remain sole scope\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"name\": \"sources\",\n              \"type\": \"ReviewSources\",\n              \"purpose\": \"One admission source session with bounded query planning, batching and memoized verified results\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"name\": \"historical\",\n              \"type\": \"boolean\",\n              \"purpose\": \"Existing historical input interpretation\",\n              \"optional\": true\n            },\n            {\n              \"name\": \"route\",\n              \"type\": \"StoryRoute\",\n              \"purpose\": \"Current host-derived workflow route\",\n              \"optional\": true\n            },\n            {\n              \"name\": \"stored\",\n              \"type\": \"StoredDerived\",\n              \"purpose\": \"Existing derived-scope evidence\",\n              \"optional\": true\n            }\n          ],\n          \"returns\": {\n            \"type\": \"Promise<PreparedReviewPacket>\",\n            \"meaning\": \"The existing full projection, tasks, committed route documents and tests, represented by an immutable prepared generation.\"\n          },\n          \"errors\": [\n            {\n              \"type\": \"TaskReviewInputError\",\n              \"condition\": \"Typed family input/context validation rejects identity, scope, capability, capacity or freshness; unknown wire input is intentional and must pass exact decoding.\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"type\": \"CheckpointSaveError | Error\",\n              \"condition\": \"Existing code atomic writer reports a definitive/uncertain save outcome; design/host/native adapters preserve their concrete Error subclasses and pointed reason, never convert unavailable proof into success.\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"preconditions\": [\n            \"Every requested object/ref is explicit and pinned; no HEAD/generic diff fallback.\",\n            \"Historical packets retain original submitted spelling and commit provenance.\"\n          ],\n          \"postconditions\": [\n            \"Current projection identity, selected spans, replacement witnesses, rename/delete lineage and test bytes match the existing correctness oracle.\",\n            \"Logical per-packet projection budgets are charged even on physical cache hits; batching does not relax scope or byte limits.\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"prepareDesignSubject\",\n          \"signature\": \"prepareDesignSubject(repo: string, artifactPath: string): PreparedDesignSubject\",\n          \"parameters\": [\n            {\n              \"name\": \"repo\",\n              \"type\": \"string\",\n              \"purpose\": \"Canonical registered project\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"name\": \"artifactPath\",\n              \"type\": \"string\",\n              \"purpose\": \"Current canonical target artifact/document locator\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            }\n          ],\n          \"returns\": {\n            \"type\": \"PreparedDesignSubject\",\n            \"meaning\": \"Fresh subject, current workflow/author resolution, baseline and inventory; any immutable reuse is subordinate to this capture.\"\n          },\n          \"errors\": [\n            {\n              \"type\": \"DesignReviewError\",\n              \"condition\": \"Typed family input/context validation rejects identity, scope, capability, capacity or freshness; unknown wire input is intentional and must pass exact decoding.\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"type\": \"CheckpointSaveError | Error\",\n              \"condition\": \"Existing code atomic writer reports a definitive/uncertain save outcome; design/host/native adapters preserve their concrete Error subclasses and pointed reason, never convert unavailable proof into success.\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"preconditions\": [\n            \"Read latest canonical artifact and document and required ancestry for the target route.\",\n            \"Do not import code-review commit pin semantics into design review.\"\n          ],\n          \"postconditions\": [\n            \"Target canonical/document changes invalidate the active attempt and require the existing human-approved restart.\",\n            \"Relevant author/route/ancestry changes invalidate the context binding. Unrelated repository changes do not invalidate the target or create restart loops.\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"ReviewWorkers\",\n          \"signature\": \"class ReviewWorkers { /* proposed additions to this existing class */ cancel(identity: ReviewWorkerIdentity, attempt: number, reason: string, context: TrustedRpcContext): Promise<ReviewCancellationReceipt>; }\",\n          \"parameters\": [\n            {\n              \"name\": \"identity\",\n              \"type\": \"ReviewWorkerIdentity\",\n              \"purpose\": \"Private exact project/family/review/worker identity\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"name\": \"attempt\",\n              \"type\": \"number\",\n              \"purpose\": \"Current attempt only\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"name\": \"reason\",\n              \"type\": \"string\",\n              \"purpose\": \"Bounded user/controller cancellation explanation\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"name\": \"context\",\n              \"type\": \"TrustedRpcContext\",\n              \"purpose\": \"Current authorized controlling connection\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            }\n          ],\n          \"returns\": {\n            \"type\": \"Promise<ReviewCancellationReceipt>\",\n            \"meaning\": \"A cancellation receipt distinguishing accepted/cancelling, stopped, and stopped-with-resource-fence; never a fabricated assessment result.\"\n          },\n          \"errors\": [\n            {\n              \"type\": \"Error\",\n              \"condition\": \"Typed family input/context validation rejects identity, scope, capability, capacity or freshness; unknown wire input is intentional and must pass exact decoding.\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"type\": \"CheckpointSaveError | Error\",\n              \"condition\": \"Existing code atomic writer reports a definitive/uncertain save outcome; design/host/native adapters preserve their concrete Error subclasses and pointed reason, never convert unavailable proof into success.\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"preconditions\": [\n            \"Resolve control authority on the main host; reject foreign connections, attempts and identities. No caller-supplied PID or clearance receipt.\",\n            \"Cancel is an explicit supported operation for each family; resource clearance remains a separate existing broker action.\"\n          ],\n          \"postconditions\": [\n            \"Durably record cancellation intent in compact runtime state, prevent further native admissions, abort only the selected native owner and terminate/reclaim its worker.\",\n            \"Report stopped only after worker exit; report fully disposed only after confirmed native closure and durable closure writes.\",\n            \"Persist/interpolate interrupted observation without changing submitted packets or prior feedback. Missing disposal confirmation retains the guard and requires explicit recovery; no auto-resume/new attempt.\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"runReviewWorker\",\n          \"signature\": \"runReviewWorker(init: ReviewWorkerInit, deps?: {readonly code?: TaskReviewDeps | undefined; readonly design?: DesignCoordinatorDeps | undefined}): Promise<void>\",\n          \"parameters\": [\n            {\n              \"name\": \"init\",\n              \"type\": \"ReviewWorkerInit\",\n              \"purpose\": \"Host-issued review/attempt/runtime/context capabilities\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"name\": \"deps\",\n              \"type\": \"{readonly code?: TaskReviewDeps | undefined; readonly design?: DesignCoordinatorDeps | undefined}\",\n              \"purpose\": \"Existing family/source/provider adapters plus private preparation/runtime adapters\",\n              \"optional\": true\n            }\n          ],\n          \"returns\": {\n            \"type\": \"Promise<void>\",\n            \"meaning\": \"One isolated family coordinator with context acquisition and compact progress publication.\"\n          },\n          \"errors\": [\n            {\n              \"type\": \"Error\",\n              \"condition\": \"Typed family input/context validation rejects identity, scope, capability, capacity or freshness; unknown wire input is intentional and must pass exact decoding.\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"type\": \"CheckpointSaveError | Error\",\n              \"condition\": \"Existing code atomic writer reports a definitive/uncertain save outcome; design/host/native adapters preserve their concrete Error subclasses and pointed reason, never convert unavailable proof into success.\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"preconditions\": [\n            \"Worker remains dedicated to one review; main host owns native leases and compact runtime writes.\",\n            \"Source preparation/qualification remains worker work; main retains only bounded registry metadata, not large source graphs.\"\n          ],\n          \"postconditions\": [\n            \"Acquire a matching context generation before judging and retain a borrow through model/native reads.\",\n            \"Release execution worker and native resources independently from retention of immutable prepared context.\",\n            \"Publish actual preparation substage, counters and cancellation state through the existing review progress path.\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"updateStoredCodeCheckpoint\",\n          \"signature\": \"updateStoredCodeCheckpoint(path: string, mutate: (current: StoredReviewCheckpoint | undefined) => StoredReviewCheckpoint | Promise<StoredReviewCheckpoint>): Promise<StoredReviewCheckpoint>\",\n          \"parameters\": [\n            {\n              \"name\": \"path\",\n              \"type\": \"string\",\n              \"purpose\": \"Canonical bounded review history file\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"name\": \"mutate\",\n              \"type\": \"typed callback\",\n              \"purpose\": \"Admission/input, accepted scope, result or publication boundary mutation\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            }\n          ],\n          \"returns\": {\n            \"type\": \"Promise<StoredReviewCheckpoint>\",\n            \"meaning\": \"Atomic full history commit at semantic boundaries, not a native-lease write.\"\n          },\n          \"errors\": [\n            {\n              \"type\": \"TaskReviewInputError\",\n              \"condition\": \"Typed family input/context validation rejects identity, scope, capability, capacity or freshness; unknown wire input is intentional and must pass exact decoding.\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"type\": \"CheckpointSaveError | Error\",\n              \"condition\": \"Existing code atomic writer reports a definitive/uncertain save outcome; design/host/native adapters preserve their concrete Error subclasses and pointed reason, never convert unavailable proof into success.\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"preconditions\": [\n            \"Existing serialized writer, no-follow checks and definitive replaced/not-replaced/uncertain outcomes remain.\",\n            \"Native hot-state readers/writers use the separate compact runtime authority after format cutover.\"\n          ],\n          \"postconditions\": [\n            \"Each attempt retains complete metadata, submitted packet and daemon response; prior pinned history is immutable.\",\n            \"History changes are source-stamp/digest guarded and invalidate affected preparation bindings; progress/native updates cannot overwrite feedback.\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"updateStoredDesignCheckpoint\",\n          \"signature\": \"updateStoredDesignCheckpoint(project: string, reviewId: string, mutate: (current: StoredDesignCheckpoint | undefined) => StoredDesignCheckpoint | Promise<StoredDesignCheckpoint>, hostConfirmedClosures?: readonly ReviewResourceGuard['openLeases'][number][], authorizedClearance?: ReviewAuthorizedClearance): Promise<StoredDesignCheckpoint>\",\n          \"parameters\": [\n            {\n              \"name\": \"project\",\n              \"type\": \"string\",\n              \"purpose\": \"Canonical project\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"name\": \"reviewId\",\n              \"type\": \"string\",\n              \"purpose\": \"Existing literal review id\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"name\": \"mutate\",\n              \"type\": \"(current: StoredDesignCheckpoint | undefined) => StoredDesignCheckpoint | Promise<StoredDesignCheckpoint>\",\n              \"purpose\": \"Attempt/chunk/feedback/action semantic boundary\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"name\": \"hostConfirmedClosures\",\n              \"type\": \"readonly Lease[]\",\n              \"purpose\": \"Historical-format normalization only; new hot closures belong to compact runtime\",\n              \"optional\": true\n            },\n            {\n              \"name\": \"authorizedClearance\",\n              \"type\": \"ReviewAuthorizedClearance\",\n              \"purpose\": \"Existing host-verified broker clearance semantics\",\n              \"optional\": true\n            }\n          ],\n          \"returns\": {\n            \"type\": \"Promise<StoredDesignCheckpoint>\",\n            \"meaning\": \"Serialized design-history commit preserving accepted chunks, actions and publication identity.\"\n          },\n          \"errors\": [\n            {\n              \"type\": \"DesignReviewError\",\n              \"condition\": \"Typed family input/context validation rejects identity, scope, capability, capacity or freshness; unknown wire input is intentional and must pass exact decoding.\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"type\": \"CheckpointSaveError | Error\",\n              \"condition\": \"Existing code atomic writer reports a definitive/uncertain save outcome; design/host/native adapters preserve their concrete Error subclasses and pointed reason, never convert unavailable proof into success.\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"preconditions\": [\n            \"Preserve exact full/impact retry and immutable action rules.\",\n            \"All resource-proof consumers agree on legacy embedded versus new runtime format; no interpretation as an empty guard.\"\n          ],\n          \"postconditions\": [\n            \"A native open/close or progress update does not rewrite reviewed canonical/document bytes.\",\n            \"Target changes still invalidate; technical retry limits and explicit user recovery decisions remain unchanged.\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"publishTaskCheckpoint\",\n          \"signature\": \"publishTaskCheckpoint(project: string, epicHash: string, reviewId: string, deps: PublicationDeps): Promise<{path: string; jsonPath: string; status: string}>\",\n          \"parameters\": [\n            {\n              \"name\": \"project\",\n              \"type\": \"string\",\n              \"purpose\": \"Registered project\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"name\": \"epicHash\",\n              \"type\": \"string\",\n              \"purpose\": \"Tracked subject root\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"name\": \"reviewId\",\n              \"type\": \"string\",\n              \"purpose\": \"Pinned review identity\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"name\": \"deps\",\n              \"type\": \"PublicationDeps\",\n              \"purpose\": \"Existing writer/sources plus private context/runtime reader\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            }\n          ],\n          \"returns\": {\n            \"type\": \"Promise<{path:string;jsonPath:string;status:string}>\",\n            \"meaning\": \"Permanent CR built from preserved terminal feedback and qualified context.\"\n          },\n          \"errors\": [\n            {\n              \"type\": \"TaskReviewInputError\",\n              \"condition\": \"Typed family input/context validation rejects identity, scope, capability, capacity or freshness; unknown wire input is intentional and must pass exact decoding.\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"type\": \"CheckpointSaveError | Error\",\n              \"condition\": \"Existing code atomic writer reports a definitive/uncertain save outcome; design/host/native adapters preserve their concrete Error subclasses and pointed reason, never convert unavailable proof into success.\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"preconditions\": [\n            \"Validate supported permanent CR capability/version and all saved origins/results.\",\n            \"Obtain a matching context binding or perform one cold bounded qualification; refresh current BUILD/author/publication authority.\"\n          ],\n          \"postconditions\": [\n            \"No provider is called by publication retry.\",\n            \"No separate repeated packet/history reconstruction occurs once the operation owns qualified context.\",\n            \"Permanent history is self-contained after temp cleanup; ephemeral context receipt is not a cross-restart approval credential.\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"publishDesignReview\",\n          \"signature\": \"publishDesignReview(input: StoredDesignCheckpoint, deps?: DesignPublicationDeps): Promise<DesignPublication>\",\n          \"parameters\": [\n            {\n              \"name\": \"input\",\n              \"type\": \"StoredDesignCheckpoint\",\n              \"purpose\": \"Terminal accepted design history\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"name\": \"deps\",\n              \"type\": \"DesignPublicationDeps\",\n              \"purpose\": \"Existing round writer plus private context/runtime reader\",\n              \"optional\": true\n            }\n          ],\n          \"returns\": {\n            \"type\": \"Promise<DesignPublication>\",\n            \"meaning\": \"Versioned complete design history preserving report, actions, failures and context identity.\"\n          },\n          \"errors\": [\n            {\n              \"type\": \"DesignReviewError\",\n              \"condition\": \"Typed family input/context validation rejects identity, scope, capability, capacity or freshness; unknown wire input is intentional and must pass exact decoding.\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"type\": \"CheckpointSaveError | Error\",\n              \"condition\": \"Existing code atomic writer reports a definitive/uncertain save outcome; design/host/native adapters preserve their concrete Error subclasses and pointed reason, never convert unavailable proof into success.\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"preconditions\": [\n            \"Recheck latest canonical target, author/route and owned bookkeeping changes separately.\",\n            \"No cached generation overrides subject invalidation or missing preserved feedback.\"\n          ],\n          \"postconditions\": [\n            \"Publication-only retry does not change assessment identity or dispatch a reviewer.\",\n            \"History supports later permanent reads without temporary context files; cleanup still requires approval and complete preservation.\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"cleanupStoryCheckpoints\",\n          \"signature\": \"cleanupStoryCheckpoints(project: string, hash: string, story: string, deps: {sources: ReviewSources; unlink?: typeof unlink; onDeleted?: (id:string)=>void; ownerReviewId?: string; preparation?: PreparationAccess}): Promise<CleanupResult>\",\n          \"parameters\": [\n            {\n              \"name\": \"project\",\n              \"type\": \"string\",\n              \"purpose\": \"Registered project\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"name\": \"hash\",\n              \"type\": \"string\",\n              \"purpose\": \"Tracked root\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"name\": \"story\",\n              \"type\": \"string\",\n              \"purpose\": \"Canonical story/task completion scope\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"name\": \"deps\",\n              \"type\": \"{sources: ReviewSources; unlink?: typeof unlink; onDeleted?: (id:string)=>void; ownerReviewId?: string; preparation?: PreparationAccess}\",\n              \"purpose\": \"Existing sources plus common context/runtime authority\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            }\n          ],\n          \"returns\": {\n            \"type\": \"Promise<CleanupResult>\",\n            \"meaning\": \"Deleted/retained/error lists for only the approved scope.\"\n          },\n          \"errors\": [\n            {\n              \"type\": \"TaskReviewInputError\",\n              \"condition\": \"Typed family input/context validation rejects identity, scope, capability, capacity or freshness; unknown wire input is intentional and must pass exact decoding.\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"type\": \"CheckpointSaveError | Error\",\n              \"condition\": \"Existing code atomic writer reports a definitive/uncertain save outcome; design/host/native adapters preserve their concrete Error subclasses and pointed reason, never convert unavailable proof into success.\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"preconditions\": [\n            \"Confirm actual BUILD approval, current independent completion evidence and supported permanent history.\",\n            \"Join context/runtime owner checks with the existing subject cleanup fence; no native/CLI/borrowed-context work may remain.\"\n          ],\n          \"postconditions\": [\n            \"Validate saved feedback, scope and capability through one qualified operation; reuse immutable context instead of independently walking all source again.\",\n            \"Remove temp history, unborrowed context and runtime only after permanent preservation and confirmed resource disposal.\",\n            \"Unknown/malformed/missing required state is retained with a pointed reason; no silent deletion or model call.\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"cleanupDesignArtifact\",\n          \"signature\": \"cleanupDesignArtifact(projectInput: string, artifactId: string, deps?: DesignCleanupDeps): Promise<CleanupResult>\",\n          \"parameters\": [\n            {\n              \"name\": \"projectInput\",\n              \"type\": \"string\",\n              \"purpose\": \"Canonical project\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"name\": \"artifactId\",\n              \"type\": \"string\",\n              \"purpose\": \"Approved DEF/HLD/LLD target\",\n              \"optional\": false\n            },\n            {\n              \"name\": \"deps\",\n              \"type\": \"DesignCleanupDeps\",\n              \"purpose\": \"Existing lifecycle plus shared context/runtime authority\",\n              \"optional\": true\n            }\n          ],\n          \"returns\": {\n            \"type\": \"Promise<CleanupResult>\",\n            \"meaning\": \"Targeted cleanup using current approval, preserved history and the same runtime proof as execution.\"\n          },\n          \"errors\": [\n            {\n              \"type\": \"DesignReviewError\",\n              \"condition\": \"Typed family input/context validation rejects identity, scope, capability, capacity or freshness; unknown wire input is intentional and must pass exact decoding.\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"type\": \"CheckpointSaveError | Error\",\n              \"condition\": \"Existing code atomic writer reports a definitive/uncertain save outcome; design/host/native adapters preserve their concrete Error subclasses and pointed reason, never convert unavailable proof into success.\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"preconditions\": [\n            \"Target approval and preserved current independent review must hold.\",\n            \"No active owner, context borrow or uncertain native lease for the target.\"\n          ],\n          \"postconditions\": [\n            \"Latest artifact checks remain distinct from immutable evidence reuse.\",\n            \"Delete derived temp state only after complete permanent preservation; unrelated targets/reviews remain unaffected.\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    \"dataModelChanges\": [\n      {\n        \"entity\": \"Review preparation lifecycle and scope matrix\",\n        \"change\": \"invariant-change\",\n        \"details\": \"IR1-IR8 derive from approved ISSUE-470a1f61b26b12c6. Stages are: durable input admission; validate current authority; inventory required evidence; fetch/qualify unique sources; construct complete task/chunk views; publish ready context; assess; preserve result; publish CR; approve; clean temp state. Every entrypoint uses this same preparation owner, not its own reconstruction loop. Code matrix: epic planned story pins DEF/story+LLD+PLAN where produced; standalone planned story pins LLD+PLAN; LLD-only story pins LLD; issue-only fix pins ISSUE; trivial/no-document scope uses tracked BUILD focus. Existing route resolver remains the authority. Story review retains all tasks; task review selects the exact task and dependencies without granting findings outside selected source. Design matrix: DEF, HLD and LLD resolve latest target/ancestry under their actual epic/standalone/issue route; no artificial HLD/DEF requirement for standalone/issues. Both daemon and controller reviewers consume equivalent prepared scope. Index impact data may augment analysis but never defines source scope or permits omission. All code refs remain committed/pinned; design target edits invalidate and require the existing user-approved restart, while unrelated repository edits are ignored.\",\n        \"callSites\": [\n          \"src/workflow/code-review/task-review/admission.ts\",\n          \"src/workflow/code-review/task-review/packet.ts\",\n          \"src/workflow/review/design-review/subject.ts\",\n          \"src/workflow/code-review/task-review/coordinator.ts\",\n          \"src/workflow/review/design-review/coordinator.ts\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"entity\": \"Prepared context generation (proposed)\",\n        \"change\": \"new\",\n        \"details\": \"Stable source generation identity binds canonical project/family/review, pinned attempt input, validator version, route, selected scope, source revision or captured latest-design identity, projection, tests and documents. Accepted feedback is excluded from this source key. Current authority/freshness remains independently checked. Exact source/input/subject changes require a new immutable generation. A separate immutable HistoryBindingV1 binds generationId, priorBindingDigest, semanticSequence, validated historyPrefixDigest, attribution/actions/results and evidenceManifestDigest. Initial qualification validates the complete prefix. Each accepted result validates new feedback/origins and any new evidence, then creates a successor history binding reusing already qualified source evidence. New evidence extends immutable evidence storage without mutating existing manifests. Earlier-history changes revoke descendant bindings and require explicit revalidation. All required projection/witness/test bytes remain complete. Storage stays in .insrc/tmp/review-context/<family>/<review-id>/ with staged-to-ready atomic publication; files alone grant no authority. Design prompts retain canonical document links rather than copied bodies.\",\n        \"callSites\": [\n          \"src/workflow/code-review/task-review/packet.ts\",\n          \"src/workflow/code-review/task-review/sources.ts\",\n          \"src/workflow/review/design-review/subject.ts\",\n          \"src/daemon/threads/review-worker-runtime.ts\"\n        ],\n        \"schemaDiff\": \"PreparedContextManifestV1 {key,generationId,inputDigest,validatorVersion,sourceIdentity,manifestDigest,objects[],views[],byteTotals}; HistoryBindingV1 {generationId,priorBindingDigest,semanticSequence,historyPrefixDigest,evidenceManifestDigest,bindingDigest}. Checkpoints reference stable source generation plus current immutable history binding.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"entity\": \"Private qualification receipt and context borrow (proposed)\",\n        \"change\": \"new\",\n        \"details\": \"Main host retains only compact process-local metadata binding an exact manifest digest/generation to the qualifying registered worker incarnation and daemon epoch. A ready receipt is accepted only over the private worker channel after current input/subject reservation checks; caller/model JSON can never supply one. Its referenced immutable bytes are verified against this expected digest when reopened. A new authorized phase worker can borrow matching context after fresh authority checks without retaining a finished execution worker. Borrow ownership is exact review/phase/incarnation; active model/native readers retain a borrow until process disposal, not merely until candidate feedback arrives. Warm reuse checks validator version, packet/history/source/route binding and immutable file identity; missing or corrupted files revoke the receipt and require controlled rebuild or a pointed failure. On daemon restart all receipts are lost: disk manifests are untrusted hints and cold qualification recomputes correctness from authoritative inputs using the batched source session. No persistent signature, HMAC, trust key or stored digest alone confers trust. An LRU/byte-cap eviction may remove only unborrowed derived context; it never deletes review inputs/results or clears resources. Same-context acquisition coalesces under one review owner; other reviews have independent context authority. Receipts separately bind stable source generation and validated history binding. Accepted result progression and publication bookkeeping advance the latter without source requalification. Fresh author/route/approval checks remain mandatory; history tampering revokes descendant bindings. Cold receipts still require qualification, never disk-digest trust.\",\n        \"callSites\": [\n          \"src/daemon/threads/review-workers.ts\",\n          \"src/daemon/threads/review-worker-runtime.ts\",\n          \"src/workflow/code-review/task-review/admission.ts\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"entity\": \"Verified source session (proposed)\",\n        \"change\": \"new\",\n        \"details\": \"A bounded source session spans all prior/current packets and reference checks required by one preparation operation. Keys include canonical project/Git identity and the complete immutable operation arguments: commit OID; commit:path; ancestor pair; diff origin/parent/exact paths/options; full-history path interval. Only successfully verified results are cached; retry/absence/error semantics are explicit, and no mutable HEAD/ref name is accepted as a reusable key. Concurrent duplicate requests coalesce, but no Promise.all is used for provider calls. Plan object reads across the inventory and use existing git_cat_file revs batches; batch independent diff/path/ancestry work only where the current validators can preserve exactly the same proof. Keep complete merge/path/delete/rename/replacement witnesses; no first-parent or lossy lineage shortcut. Discovery can add bounded queries to the plan; total stays unknown until determined. Share raw verified reads across packets; retain independent logical source/fragment/byte accounting for each packet so reuse never bypasses existing ProjectionBudget or scope checks. Query output order and error field attribution remain deterministic. Configuration is limited to review.preparation batchMaxObjects(default256), batchMaxBytes(default4MiB), memoryMaxBytes(default64MiB) and cacheMaxBytes(default256MiB), all validated positive safe bounds and clamped by existing per-object/tool/projection limits; configurable lower values may split work or cause explicit capacity failure, never truncate evidence. A single valid object above a batch target is read alone within existing object/remaining-total limits. Existing review.maxJsonBytes continues governing JSON envelopes. Source work stays isolated/read-only through existing host authorization; pooling does not create a worker-local native bypass. Per-session retention: successfully verified query results are durably staged with an exact query index and immutable payload before memory eviction. Memory LRU drops decoded bytes only; subsequent consumers verify/reopen retained staging, never refetch Git. Pin all evidence needed by unfinished packet consumers against disk eviction. Session staging, manifests, ready context and temporary duplicate bytes all count against cacheMaxBytes; decoded bytes count against memoryMaxBytes. A serialized per-project capacity allocator accounts concurrent sessions, reserves bounded space before each batch and grows reservations incrementally for unknown inventory; it may evict only inactive unborrowed generations. If pinned evidence plus next batch cannot fit, fail precisely before discarding evidence or spawning the batch. No indefinite capacity wait, silent refetch, truncation or implicit limit increase. Release abandoned staging only after exact owned readers/resources are disposed. This makes the zero-duplicate guarantee hold under memory pressure.\",\n        \"callSites\": [\n          \"src/workflow/code-review/task-review/sources.ts\",\n          \"src/workflow/code-review/task-review/packet.ts\",\n          \"src/workflow/code-review/task-review/admission.ts\",\n          \"src/daemon/threads/review-native-host.ts\",\n          \"src/daemon/threads/review-processes.ts\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"entity\": \"Review history and compact runtime state (proposed)\",\n        \"change\": \"invariant-change\",\n        \"details\": \"Retain full per-attempt header, submitted packet and review response in existing project checkpoint paths. Introduce checkpoint format3 for each family with runtime/context references; new executions write only the new format after reader cutover. Main host is the sole authoritative writer of a proposed compact .insrc/tmp/review-runtime/<family>/<review-id>.json record. RuntimeV1 binds project/family/review/attempt, runtimeId, daemon/worker incarnation, acknowledged checkpoint/input digest and sequence, lifecycle state, bounded open leases/clearance, current progress/cancellation, and durable result/publication boundary references. Maximum encoded runtime size is256KiB, checked against bounded field/lease counts; no input packet, source blob, complete history or full review response is allowed there. Critical lease/cancel/result-boundary updates are serialized and atomically synchronized; observational progress is coalesced at250ms and flushed at phase boundaries. Full checkpoint writes occur at admission, accepted plan/scope, task/chunk result and publication/approval semantic boundaries, not every source operation. Progress reads use compact runtime and immutable counts; full history is decoded only when a new semantic generation or requested result requires it. Controlled file stamps plus content binding detect external checkpoint replacement and revoke affected authority; native admission/phase boundaries cannot continue on changed pinned input. Never cache mutable author, approval, route or artifact freshness. checkpointBinding distinguishes stable source/input identity from the current validated semantic history binding. Normal accepted feedback advances only the history binding; runtime completion references that exact successor.\",\n        \"callSites\": [\n          \"src/workflow/code-review/task-review/checkpoint.ts\",\n          \"src/workflow/review/design-review/checkpoint.ts\",\n          \"src/daemon/threads/review-worker-resources.ts\",\n          \"src/daemon/threads/review-worker-runtime.ts\",\n          \"src/daemon/threads/review-workers.ts\"\n        ],\n        \"schemaDiff\": \"Proposed ReviewRuntimeV1 {key, attempt, runtimeId, daemonEpoch, workerIncarnation, checkpointBinding, sequence, state, resourceGuard, preparation, progress, cancellation?, committedResultBoundary?, publicationBoundary?}; schema exact, no arbitrary paths/PIDs from clients. Runtime reference is a derived canonical locator, not a caller-selected file.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"entity\": \"Cross-store commit and native durability ordering\",\n        \"change\": \"invariant-change\",\n        \"details\": \"Initialization order: create an initializing empty runtime record under the host's exact scope reservation; durably append full attempt input plus matching runtime reference to the checkpoint; bind that confirmed checkpoint/input receipt and activate runtime; acknowledge admission; schedule preparation. An orphan initializing runtime cannot spawn; a checkpoint with incomplete/mismatched runtime cannot execute and requires explicit initialization recovery. Resolve uncertain writes using the existing definitive atomic-write outcomes, never by assuming rollback. For each native command: durably add its exact open intent to compact runtime BEFORE spawn authorization; only after host-confirmed process/group disposal may a durable close remove that lease. No asynchronous fire-and-forget durability. Result order: checkpoint contains complete accepted feedback first; runtime advances its committed result boundary afterward. A crash between these writes is reconciled from validated checkpoint evidence without rerunning a completed task; runtime never independently asserts a result absent from history. Publication follows the analogous permanent-CR commit then durable publication boundary. Context ready order: complete/verify immutable files, atomically publish ready manifest, receive private qualification receipt, then expose a usable handle. Cancellation revokes admission before draining native work and worker exit. These transitions share per-review serialization with cleanup; no global review lock or shared daemon-thread LLM work. For result commits, validate feedback/origins and new evidence, stage the immutable successor history binding, atomically commit feedback plus its binding reference in the checkpoint, then advance runtime. Unreferenced staged bindings grant no authority. Reconcile a committed referenced binding by validating its history delta against the prior binding; never rerun a model solely for this reconciliation.\",\n        \"callSites\": [\n          \"src/daemon/threads/review-worker-resources.ts\",\n          \"src/daemon/threads/review-native-host.ts\",\n          \"src/daemon/threads/review-processes.ts\",\n          \"src/workflow/code-review/task-review/checkpoint.ts\",\n          \"src/workflow/review/design-review/checkpoint.ts\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"entity\": \"Preparation progress and public cancellation contract\",\n        \"change\": \"field-add\",\n        \"details\": \"Keep existing status enums and phase meaning; expose preparation details as bounded optional progress fields with a typed stage(validate_input, inspect_history, source_inventory, fetch_sources, qualify_scope, build_views, commit_context), logical/physical completed counts, cache hits, bytes, elapsed time and a nullable known total. Do not invent percentages or selected task/chunk counts before qualification. Real completed validation/native work updates meaningful activity; waiting for a long-running tool remains explicitly tracked, and timer-only heartbeat does not masquerade as progress. Target progress observation gap<=2s under the controlled qualification workload. Add explicit cancel phases to code/design review MCP schemas and corresponding registered daemon operations with repo/reviewId/attempt/reason only. Host derives control ownership; return accepted/cancelling promptly and publish stopped/resource_fenced only after observed outcomes. Old request fields remain rejected; no caller-supplied source context authority, PID or approval receipt. Align shared IPC/DTO validation for the current VS Code and JetBrains clients and MCP consumers; no new IDE layout/button or deprecated insrc-ide integration is included. New progress/format capability is advertised at reconnect; unsupported required formats fail clearly rather than silently entering an old engine.\",\n        \"callSites\": [\n          \"src/workflow/code-review/task-review/progress.ts\",\n          \"src/workflow/code-review/task-review/contracts.ts\",\n          \"src/workflow/review/design-review/contracts.ts\",\n          \"src/daemon/threads/review-worker-runtime.ts\",\n          \"src/daemon/threads/review-workers.ts\",\n          \"src/daemon/review-service.ts\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"entity\": \"Ownership, retention and cleanup relationships\",\n        \"change\": \"invariant-change\",\n        \"details\": \"One ReviewSession owns one full checkpoint with1..N immutable numbered attempts and at most1 active runtime writer/worker incarnation. Each attempt may reference0..1 stable ready source generation and, once qualified,1..N immutable successor history bindings; no ready context is required before unverified admission. One generation contains1..N bounded immutable evidence objects/views and may have0..N phase borrows. A daemon receipt references exactly1 generation/digest and is not persisted as an authorization credential. Current runtime references exactly1 current attempt; resource leases are owned by its exact worker incarnation and may outlive worker loss as a recovery fence. Context retention does not retain subject admission exclusions or terminal execution workers. Cleanup first acquires the existing target scope fence and checks approval/permanent preservation, no active owner/borrow/publication and no uncertain leases. It then releases receipt/borrows, removes inactive derived files and runtime after required audit preservation, and deletes working checkpoints last; failed partial cleanup is idempotently retriable with retained diagnostics. Permanent CR must retain complete submitted scopes, feedback, origins and admission/technical failures and bounded final operational audit, not references to deletable temp bytes. Proposed code CR format4 and design CR format3 carry the new runtime audit/binding capability; historical supported CR formats remain read-only. Post-cleanup progress reads permanent history with explicit locator and no model/rebuild. Completion of this correction's BUILD does not complete or approve BUILD-e4af63128c7cbec2-s1. The existing committed worker implementation is a dependency under qualification, not declared independently approved. After deployment, an explicitly authorized next attempt must use a newly committed packet/current source pin if sources changed, including relevant selected replacement witnesses; the canceled attempt4 input remains immutable. These explicit cardinalities are normative. The optional ER rendering is omitted because the current companion renderer draws required-many edges as optional-many despite source minima; the sequence and component views plus this complete ownership/cardinality contract are sufficient to assess the model without a misleading ER view. Cleanup requires a durable CleanupClaimV1 before deleting any runtime/context/checkpoint file, extending existing design private claims to both families. Under the target fence, first preserve exact closed resource audit and cleanup eligibility in permanent history; atomically persist/sync the claim binding project/family/review, checkpoint digest/file identity, runtimeId/closed-audit digest, source/history bindings, approval revision, permanent preservation receipt/digest and bounded exact deletion inventory. Claim ownership permits cleanup only, never execution/admission. Delete disposable context/runtime and then claimed checkpoint last, syncing affected directories; delete the claim last. After a crash an explicit cleanup retry validates current approval, permanent preservation and claim, then finishes only its exact remaining deletions without source/model calls. Missing runtime is accepted exclusively in this cleanup-only path with matching claim and permanent closed audit; normal execution/recovery still fences missing runtime. Replaced/mismatched files are retained. A crash after checkpoint deletion is recoverable from claim plus permanent record. No new trust keys/event store.\",\n        \"callSites\": [\n          \"src/workflow/code-review/task-review/publication.ts\",\n          \"src/workflow/review/design-review/publication.ts\",\n          \"src/workflow/code-review/task-review/cleanup.ts\",\n          \"src/workflow/review/design-review/cleanup.ts\",\n          \"src/daemon/threads/review-workers.ts\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"entity\": \"Performance and correctness qualification contract\",\n        \"change\": \"invariant-change\",\n        \"details\": \"Release gates are measurements, not runtime deadlines. On the retained171-file/four-attempt workload, three controlled runs under the supported Node/native build must show cold full managed preparation median<=120s and warm matching-context handoff/phase preparation median<=10s, with no scope/provenance/coverage loss. Record hardware, load, baseline, cache state, timings for history validation/source acquisition/projection/context writes/runtime persistence separately, native command count and bytes written. Unique query accounting must demonstrate no physical duplicate across the preparation session; full checkpoint writes per native command must be0; operational write size is bounded independently of history growth. Warm matching publication/cleanup must use the context contract without source reconstruction; a cold restart is explicitly labelled and performs bounded requalification. Two concurrent reviews must preserve independent progress/cancel/recovery and admit/cancel acknowledgement<=2s in the controlled fixture; no performance check may be made to pass by dropping modules, ancestry, selected blocks, tests, validation or honest errors. These targets need implementation measurements and are not claimed achieved. If they fail, do not resume the blocked worker-isolation qualification or substitute a higher timeout; revise the same holistic design/plan.\",\n        \"callSites\": [\n          \"src/workflow/code-review/task-review/__tests__/projection-lineage.test.ts\",\n          \"src/workflow/code-review/task-review/__tests__/route-admission.test.ts\",\n          \"src/daemon/threads/__tests__/review-worker-isolation.test.ts\",\n          \"src/daemon/threads/__tests__/review-worker-recovery.test.ts\",\n          \"src/daemon/threads/__tests__/review-worker-publication.test.ts\",\n          \"src/daemon/threads/__tests__/review-worker-cleanup.test.ts\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"entity\": \"Private preparation access and cancellation receipt (proposed)\",\n        \"change\": \"new\",\n        \"details\": \"PreparationAccess is a private serializable capability reference issued by the main host: capabilityId, daemonEpoch and optional expectedGenerationId. It is resolved only through the owning private worker connection and is never accepted from public input; no closure or large source graph crosses the port. ReviewAdmissionContext, family publication/cleanup dependencies and worker bootstrap data carry this reference, with no behavioral legacy fallback: absent private reuse authority takes the same cold qualification path. ReviewCancellationReceipt contains exact reviewId/attempt/action identity and operationState(cancelling|stopped|resource_fenced), plus durable observation/remaining-resource metadata. The review's existing status enum is unchanged; operational cancellation state is separate. Runtime for a later attempt may replace only an inactive prior runtime after its exact final closed audit is committed in history; unresolved earlier leases prohibit replacement. Root runtime files remain bounded while older closed audit summaries live at semantic history boundaries.\",\n        \"callSites\": [\n          \"src/daemon/threads/review-workers.ts\",\n          \"src/daemon/threads/review-worker-runtime.ts\",\n          \"src/workflow/code-review/task-review/admission.ts\",\n          \"src/workflow/code-review/task-review/publication.ts\",\n          \"src/workflow/review/design-review/publication.ts\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"entity\": \"Bounded prepared packet views and working-set ownership (revision)\",\n        \"change\": \"invariant-change\",\n        \"details\": \"Replace CodePreparation's eager Map<string,PreparedReviewPacket> payloads and whole 'code-packets' view with a bounded digest index and staged per-packet/task/file metadata plus content-addressed text/binary leaves in the existing review-context generation. One generation owns many packet descriptors; one descriptor identifies exactly one submitted/historical/route/derived tuple; task descriptors reference every selected change and exact provenance witness, tests and document refs without copying leaf payloads. Leaves can be referenced by many descriptors; generation owns immutable leaf lifetime, phase borrows pin generation until disposal. No reference crosses a generation's digest allowlist. Disk alone remains non-authoritative. Descriptor order, explicit null/undefined, array order, Unicode, Uint8Array and exact source OIDs survive round-trip. Hash canonical metadata with digest references, never JSON numeric-array encodings of payloads. No eager aggregate packets/inputs/clone just to derive source/scope/test identities: fold ordered descriptors incrementally with explicit domain/version and verify the same logical inputs. No changed selection, generic HEAD scope, history prefix or result omission. Stage each qualified validation window before retaining the next; validate current/historical packets and all feedback/origins in sequence. Pure final-scope/projection validators consume pinned source handles and bounded windows, retaining only bounded indexes/lineage metadata; after/before blobs and replacement/merge witnesses stay staged and are opened as required. Before/after provenance witnesses are not added to reviewer prompt scope. Execution/prompt/test coverage/publication/recovery consume task/file windows and release before the next; whole-story scope is traversed completely, not sampled. Do not implement a lazy wrapper that later materializes an oversized task or packet. Code and design readers share bounded codec/accounting. Existing small caller shape may be adapted but there is one qualified implementation and no unbounded compatibility fallback. memoryMaxBytes remains64MiB by default and bounds charged preparation buffers/decoded leaves/strings/indexes/descriptors/active consumer allocations together per phase; binary byteLength once per shared backing allocation, text conservative UTF-16 plus encoding/transient copies, bounded metadata overhead, reserve before allocate/read/clone/parse. Include writer/decoder scratch and concurrent source/consumer reservations; evict only unborrowed decoded data, keep reserved disk evidence. Release charges after last owner/reference, not while views remain reachable. Reject genuinely unrepresentable atomic units before allocation with a pointed capacity error; do not raise caps or drop content. Report memory high-water charged bytes versus actual heap/external/RSS separately; RSS is diagnostic, not falsely described as the configured whole-process cap. Streaming encoder/decoder chunks and descriptor index shards stay within batchMaxBytes and memoryMaxBytes. Reserve new disk objects before writes through existing host aggregate capacity, dedup content once; context sealing promotes/reuses staged leaves instead of copying the entire history twice. Manifest/index schemas explicitly version changed encoding; old derived generations are disposable and cold-requalified with exact history/native recovery gates, never accepted by an older decoder. No checkpoint/CR schema bump merely for derived storage. Per-view hashes, structural limits/depth/count checks, safe paths, atomic stage-to-ready, partial-write cleanup, no source/model side effects before proof, receipt/epoch checks and cleanup claims remain normative.\",\n        \"callSites\": [\n          \"src/workflow/review/code-preparation.ts\",\n          \"src/workflow/review/prepared-context.ts\",\n          \"src/workflow/review/source-session.ts\",\n          \"src/workflow/code-review/task-review/packet.ts\",\n          \"src/workflow/code-review/task-review/projection.ts\",\n          \"src/workflow/code-review/task-review/admission.ts\",\n          \"src/workflow/code-review/task-review/worker-checkpoint.ts\",\n          \"src/workflow/code-review/task-review/execution.ts\",\n          \"src/workf