ins fenced.\"\n          ],\n          \"fixturesNeeded\": [\n            \"Existing checkpoint-outcomes, pending-failure-history, design checkpoint/recovery/subject-monitor suites; literal file-byte preservation assertions.\",\n            \"Detached fake native process groups and injected synchronization outcomes; full CLI/process inventory limited to disposable owned fixtures.\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"level\": \"integration\",\n          \"purpose\": \"Release-blocking preparation performance and scaling qualification on the managed pipeline.\",\n          \"subjects\": [\n            \"Capture three cold runs of the complete171-file/four-attempt workload: median preparation<=120s with every source, scope, origin, test and history check retained; report each run and host/load metadata.\",\n            \"Warm matching-context lifecycle handoff/phase preparation median<=10s; matching publication/cleanup performs0 source reconstructions while current mutable checks still run.\",\n            \"Growing valid history at1,4 and maximum supported attempts: physical repeated queries per session0, immutable source work proportional to distinct evidence plus history validation, not repeated packet count.\",\n            \"Full checkpoint writes per native command0; compact runtime encoder<=256KiB and write size does not grow with history/source size. Report native command counts, total bytes written and stage timings separately.\",\n            \"Two concurrent reviews admit/cancel acknowledgement<=2s and preparation observation gap<=2s on the controlled supported-host fixture; cancellation reaches an honest stopped or resource-fenced result without another model call.\",\n            \"No timing assertion is a fixed runtime task deadline. If a release gate fails, report the measured failure; do not skip tests, widen timeouts/limits, shrink scope or claim the microbenchmark substitutes for this evidence.\",\n            \"Working set above memoryM