   \"migration\": {\n      \"stateBefore\": \"As established by s1.analyzeBundles[0]-[2], code admission/publication/cleanup reconstruct historical source packets, design preparation captures latest target/ancestry, and native resource mutations use full family checkpoint writers. Existing stored code/design formats include qualified v1 and admission-aware v2 with embedded guards; permanent CR capability readers distinguish supported history versions. Progress stays at scope_preparation while source work executes. s1.analyzeBundles[3] records the actual stopped attempt4 and measured overhead. That stopped checkpoint and all other review histories must remain intact. Revision baseline: t1-t13 implementation and passing focused records exist; t14 failed the retained production workload before provider readiness at98328304 estimated packet bytes with64MiB cap and2831ms admission. Compact native durability and source dedup passed their observed checks; this is not full qualification.\",\n      \"stateAfter\": \"New executions use one preparation/context lifecycle and new family checkpoint format3, bounded RuntimeV1 and a versioned derived PreparedContextManifest whose new staged packet/index encoding is distinguished from the former eager-view encoding. The main host owns compact runtime writes and private current-epoch qualification receipts; immutable files alone grant no trust. Existing coordinators, complete pinned input/response history, code scope proof, latest-design invalidation, process-intent durability and human approval remain. Supported old formats are read-only inputs to explicit migration/qualification, not another execution engine. Permanent publication uses explicit new code CR4/design CR3 capability records when new runtime audit/binding data is present; old completed records remain unchanged. Stable source qualification is separate from successor history bindings; per-session disk staging retains verified queries under memory pressure; durable CleanupClaimV1 permits cleanup-only crash reconciliation. Prepared descriptors and leaves are staged during construction and consumed in bounded windows throughout lifecycle; existing source/history/runtime authority is unchanged. Revision does not reset completed task records or turn their prior evidence into proof of new behavior.\",\n      \"migrationSteps\": [\n        {\n          \"order\": 1,\n          \"action\": \"Retain a reproducible controlled fixture manifest and baseline measurements from the171-file/four-attempt workload and approved issue before relying on temporary profiling files. Inventory supported checkpoint/CR variants, current live owners and exact unresolved guards. Do not restart the stopped worker-isolation review.\",\n          \"rollbackable\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"order\": 2,\n          \"action\": \"Deliver exact versioned decoders, common operational-proof reads and context authority contracts before enabling new writes in the same final cutover. Preserve existing supported historical records and reject unknown/mismatched capabilities. Add production-route, byte-preservation and fault-window fixtures; no compatibility execution engine or feature/activation flag.\",\n          \"rollbackable\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"order\": 3,\n          \"action\": \"Implement unified source/context acquisition, compact runtime durability, lifecycle consumers and supported cancel/progress surfaces together in the tracked build sequence. During development validate new behavior in isolated source/compiled fixtures; do not partially deploy cache-only or writer-only changes to the user's daemon. Include successor history binding, aggregate disk reservation/staging retention, and both-family durable cleanup claims in the same cutover; no feedback-key or missing-runtime cleanup fallback.\",\n          \"rollbackable\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"order\": 4,\n          \"action\": \"Before final performance qualification, extend the same approved LLD/PLAN with sequenced corrective tasks for bounded typed codec/index storage, incremental projection/packet consumers, all lifecycle reads, admission attribution/correction and regression tests. Preserve t1-t13 ids/history; keep t14 qualification incomplete until corrections pass. No production implementation before revised artifacts are reviewed/presented and explicitly approved.\",\n          \"rollbackable\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"order\": 5,\n          \"action\": \"Cut over prepared-view writer and every cold/warm consumer together in isolated fixtures. Explicitly version the changed derived manifest/index encoding. Reject old derived views as qualification; retain history/runtime and exact unresolved leases and require normal cold requalification under existing authority. Do not transform pinned checkpoint inputs/results or permanent CRs, add an old eager fallback, trust persisted hashes after restart or erase an active borrow. Remove only proven inactive disposable generations under existing cleanup/capacity rules.\",\n          \"rollbackable\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"order\": 6,\n          \"action\": \"Qualify exact scope equivalence and all failure/route matrices, then the managed native cold/warm/history-growth/concurrent performance gates. Complete the required independent code review and human BUILD approval before publishing. A failed performance or correctness gate blocks returning to worker-isolation qualification.\",\n          \"rollbackable\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"order\": 7,\n          \"action\": \"Coordinate other active reviews and retain their checkpoints before the explicit approved daemon update/restart. Update daemon and required MCP/IPC/IDE DTO readers together and reconnect consumers; advertise supported new preparation/runtime/cancel capabilities. This needs a coordinated restart and does not promise zero downtime or in-flight completion.\",\n          \"rollbackable\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"order\": 8,\n          \"action\": \"On explicit use of a supported old inactive review, acquire its exact owner/target fence, validate old input/history and all embedded resource guards, create an initializing RuntimeV1, commit the upgraded format3 reference preserving submitted/results/actions byte values, then activate only a proven common binding. Preserve original migration evidence until successful completion/cleanup. Any unresolved old/native guard or uncertain write blocks activation and requires existing explicit resource recovery; never replace it with an empty guard. No automatic bulk rewrite of completed permanent CRs.\",\n          \"rollbackable\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"order\": 9,\n          \"action\": \"At cold daemon startup invalidate private qualification receipts. Treat retained manifests as untrusted hints; first authorized phase reconstructs/qualifies required immutable evidence once through the bounded source session and refreshes current authority/content. Reconcile a committed result/publication boundary from preserved checkpoint/CR evidence without invoking a model solely for bookkeeping. No automatic resume or new attempt.\",\n          \"rollbackable\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"order\": 10,\n          \"action\": \"Perform post-deployment controlled code/design smoke: preparation progress, cancel one review while another proceeds, resource fence/recovery, publication and approved cleanup. Then explicitly resolve the stopped worker-isolation review's retained guard through supported recovery and obtain the user decision to retrigger the appropriate attempt; do not count its canceled run as a completed review. If code/input changed, submit a newly committed packet and new pinned attempt; never mutate canceled attempt4. This fix's approval does not automatically complete the older BUILD.\",\n          \"rollbackable\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"order\": 11,\n          \"action\": \"Rollback before new-format emission can restore the previous binary. After format3/runtime/new-CR records exist, do not run old-only readers or reverse-transform live records: roll forward or use a state-preserving rollback build that retains new readers and leaves incomplete reviews explicitly interrupted. Permanent approved history is never rewritten as rollback; deleting unborrowed derived cache is safe but may require cold requalification.\",\n          \"rollbackable\": false\n        }\n      ],\n      \"backwardCompat\": \"Historical supported checkpoint/CR data stays readable and immutable unless an explicit inactive-checkpoint migration is required for new execution. New code/design cancel phases and optional preparation progress fields are additive for discovery-capable consumers; required new storage/runtime authority must be understood end to end. Unknown required format/capability fails clearly, never masquerades as an empty guard or older engine. Maintain aligned supported VS Code/JetBrains IPC DTOs and MCP schemas; no deprecated insrc-ide requirement. Keep full per-attempt packets and accepted feedback exactly; aliases and old action/publication history are not normalized away. No new trust keys, compatibility flags or parallel legacy execution path. A raw persisted manifest/hash is not a cross-restart qualification credential. Once new runtime/CR formats are emitted, old-only reader rollback is unsupported. This revision changes disposable prepared-view encoding only: no extra checkpoint/CR schema change solely for staging. Old eager derived views cannot be read as the new format; compatible history/runtime readers remain required for explicit cold recovery.\",\n      \"zeroDowntime\": false,\n      \"dataRewriteRequired\": true\n    },\n    \"alternativesConsidered\": [\n      {\n        \"id\": \"a1\",\n        \"name\": \"Bounded prepared-view staging in the existing context store\",\n        \"oneLineSummary\": \"Stream packet metadata and content-addressed leaves to the existing reserved context files; access only the current task or validation window.\",\n        \"approach\": \"Reuse existing typed-byte content codec, private qualification receipt, source staging and host capacity reservation. Replace eager packet inventory/whole-view loading with digest-indexed metadata and demand-loaded bounded task/file windows across preparation, history verification, execution, publication and recovery. Admission timing is traced and expensive derivation stays in registered worker paths; acknowledgement never grants qualified authority.\",\n        \"pros\": [\n          \"Smallest coherent extension preserving current lifecycle and complete scope\",\n          \"Binary/text content deduplicates without JSON numeric-array expansion\",\n          \"Cold and warm consumers obey the same working-set bound\"\n        ],\n        \"cons\": [\n          \"All eager consumers must be converted together\",\n          \"Transient projection/clone/serialization allocations need explicit budget ownership and tests\"\n        ],\n        \"costEstimate\": \"M\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"a2\",\n        \"name\": \"Dedicated disk-backed packet database\",\n        \"oneLineSummary\": \"Store packets and leaf references in a separate embedded transactional database.\",\n        \"approach\": \"Introduce a worker-local persistent database and typed records for packet indexes, scoped leaves and bounded cursor queries, retaining existing host qualification and generation identities.\",\n        \"pros\": [\n          \"Native bounded cursors and indexed retrieval\",\n          \"Transactional record boundaries\"\n        ],\n        \"cons\": [\n          \"Adds storage dependency/lifecycle/migration and packaging complexity alongside an existing adequate context store\",\n          \"Does not by itself fix eager projection or admission work\"\n        ],\n        \"costEstimate\": \"L\",\n        \"reasonRejected\": \"Duplicates existing immutable context store and adds storage/migration complexity while still requiring bounded consumer conversion.\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"chosenAlternative\": \"a1\",\n    \"openQuestions\": [],\n    \"sequenceDefinition\": {\n      \"id\": \"review-preparation-order\",\n      \"narrative\": \"The cold path makes input admission, native intent durability, context readiness and committed feedback distinct boundaries. Warm reuse skips source reconstruction only with a current private qualification receipt plus fresh authority checks; cancellation can fence the host/native owner at any phase and never invents rollback of a committed result. Revised packet staging occurs as each semantic validation window completes; no whole packet inventory is hydrated on readiness or warm borrow.\",\n      \"participants\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"controller\",\n          \"label\": \"Human / controller\",\n          \"description\": \"Controller submits exact input and carries explicit human approval/recovery decisions.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"host\",\n          \"label\": \"Main review host\",\n          \"description\": \"Owns exact scope, small runtime writer, private receipts and native process authority.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"worker\",\n          \"label\": \"Dedicated review worker\",\n          \"description\": \"Performs qualification/projection and runs the existing family coordinator.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"files\",\n          \"label\": \"Project durable files\",\n          \"description\": \"Separate history, compact runtime, derived context and permanent CR; each has its declared writer.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"git\",\n          \"label\": \"Isolated native Git\",\n          \"description\": \"Bounded pinned source operations under durable host process leases.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"reviewer\",\n          \"label\": \"Independent reviewer\",\n          \"description\": \"Existing daemon CLI or trusted controller; scope and mandatory coverage remain unchanged.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"messages\": [\n        {\n          \"from\": \"controller\",\n          \"to\": \"host\",\n          \"label\": \"Submit exact review / attempt\",\n          \"description\": \"No arbitrary source authority, PID or cached approval is accepted.\",\n          \"kind\": \"call\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"from\": \"host\",\n          \"to\": \"files\",\n          \"label\": \"Create initializing RuntimeV1\",\n          \"description\": \"Empty and inactive; cannot authorize native work.\",\n          \"kind\": \"call\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"from\": \"host\",\n          \"to\": \"worker\",\n          \"label\": \"Reserve input writer for exact owner\",\n          \"description\": \"No source or model work yet.\",\n          \"kind\": \"call\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"from\": \"worker\",\n          \"to\": \"files\",\n          \"label\": \"Commit full attempt input + runtime reference\",\n          \"description\": \"Keep complete pinned packet and history.\",\n          \"kind\": \"call\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"from\": \"worker\",\n          \"to\": \"host\",\n          \"label\": \"Return durable input binding\",\n          \"description\": \"Private acknowledged checkpoint identity.\",\n          \"kind\": \"call\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"from\": \"host\",\n          \"to\": \"files\",\n          \"label\": \"Activate matching runtime\",\n          \"description\": \"Both stores must agree before acknowledgement.\",\n          \"kind\": \"call\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"from\": \"host\",\n          \"to\": \"controller\",\n          \"label\": \"Acknowledge admission\",\n          \"description\": \"Preparation runs in background.\",\n          \"kind\": \"return\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"from\": \"host\",\n          \"to\": \"worker\",\n          \"label\": \"Acquire / prepare context\",\n          \"description\": \"Refresh author, route and family-specific subject authority.\",\n          \"kind\": \"call\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"from\": \"worker\",\n          \"to\": \"host\",\n          \"label\": \"Request bounded pinned source batch\",\n          \"description\": \"A shared source session covers history/current input.\",\n          \"kind\": \"call\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"from\": \"host\",\n          \"to\": \"files\",\n          \"label\": \"Persist exact open intent\",\n          \"description\": \"No spawn before confirmed durable intent.\",\n          \"kind\": \"call\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"from\": \"host\",\n          \"to\": \"git\",\n          \"label\": \"Run isolated bounded batch\",\n          \"description\": \"No generic HEAD diff, inherited unsafe Git environment or native bypass.\",\n          \"kind\": \"call\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"from\": \"git\",\n          \"to\": \"host\",\n          \"label\": \"Return bytes and confirmed disposal\",\n          \"description\": \"Missing/truncated/unverifiable output is not accepted as proof.\",\n          \"kind\": \"return\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"from\": \"host\",\n          \"to\": \"files\",\n          \"label\": \"Persist exact closure\",\n          \"description\": \"Uncertainty retains the resource fence.\",\n          \"kind\": \"call\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"from\": \"host\",\n          \"to\": \"worker\",\n          \"label\": \"Deliver bounded source result\",\n          \"description\": \"Worker verifies complete scope/objects/projection.\",\n          \"kind\": \"return\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"from\": \"worker\",\n          \"to\": \"files\",\n          \"label\": \"Stage bounded packet/task descriptors and leaves\",\n          \"description\": \"Charge all live buffers/indexes/scratch before allocation; release each validation window, retain complete staged evidence under aggregate disk reservation.\",\n          \"kind\": \"call\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"from\": \"worker\",\n          \"to\": \"files\",\n          \"label\": \"Commit immutable ready context\",\n          \"description\": \"Complete derived bytes and manifest, not approval authority.\",\n          \"kind\": \"call\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"from\": \"worker\",\n          \"to\": \"host\",\n          \"label\": \"Register qualified generation digest\",\n          \"description\": \"Private current owner/epoch only.\",\n          \"kind\": \"call\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"from\": \"host\",\n          \"to\": \"worker\",\n          \"label\": \"Issue context capability / borrow\",\n          \"description\": \"Main retains compact expected digest, not large source objects.\",\n          \"kind\": \"return\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"from\": \"worker\",\n          \"to\": \"reviewer\",\n          \"label\": \"Review task or chunk using context\",\n          \"description\": \"Only qualified selected scope and current design paths; no copied design body.\",\n          \"kind\": \"call\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"from\": \"reviewer\",\n          \"to\": \"worker\",\n          \"label\": \"Return feedback and coverage assessment\",\n          \"description\": \"Existing independent judge/result semantics.\",\n          \"kind\": \"return\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"from\": \"worker\",\n          \"to\": \"files\",\n          \"label\": \"Commit full accepted result\",\n          \"description\": \"Validate feedback/origins and new evidence; commit accepted history plus immutable successor history binding, reusing stable source qualification.\",\n          \"kind\": \"call\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"from\": \"worker\",\n          \"to\": \"host\",\n          \"label\": \"Confirm committed result boundary\",\n          \"description\": \"Late or canceled generations cannot advance it.\",\n          \"kind\": \"call\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"from\": \"host\",\n          \"to\": \"files\",\n          \"label\": \"Advance compact progress boundary\",\n          \"description\": \"Actual durable completion only.\",\n          \"kind\": \"call\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"from\": \"worker\",\n          \"to\": \"files\",\n          \"label\": \"Publish self-contained permanent CR\",\n          \"description\": \"No model call on publication-only retry.\",\n          \"kind\": \"call\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"from\": \"host\",\n          \"to\": \"controller\",\n          \"label\": \"Report complete result; await approval\",\n          \"description\": \"A checkpoint or private receipt is not human approval.\",\n          \"kind\": \"return\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"from\": \"controller\",\n          \"to\": \"host\",\n          \"label\": \"Explicit human approval\",\n          \"description\": \"Normal workflow gate only.\",\n          \"kind\": \"call\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"from\": \"host\",\n          \"to\": \"files\",\n          \"label\": \"Verify preservation and dispose inactive temp state\",\n          \"description\": \"Preserve closed audit, durably sync exact cleanup-only claim, remove disposable state then checkpoint, and remove claim last; explicit crash retry uses permanent proof.\",\n          \"kind\": \"call\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    \"componentDependencyDefinition\": {\n      \"id\": \"review-preparation-components\",\n      \"narrative\": \"Existing family coordinators consume one preparation boundary. The main host keeps only current authority/receipts and small runtime state; full history and immutable context remain project files, and every native source operation still crosses existing host process control.\",\n      \"components\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"surface\",\n          \"label\": \"MCP / supported IPC\",\n          \"description\": \"Submit, progress, cancel and explicit recovery contracts.\",\n          \"path\": \"src/mcp\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"host\",\n          \"label\": \"Review ownership and receipts\",\n          \"description\": \"Existing main registry with compact private preparation capabilities.\",\n          \"path\": \"src/daemon/threads/review-workers.ts\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"runtime\",\n          \"label\": \"Compact runtime authority\",\n          \"description\": \"Proposed host-owned small state writer, replacing hot full-history mutations.\",\n          \"path\": \"src/daemon/threads/review-worker-resources.ts\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"worker\",\n          \"label\": \"Family coordinator workers\",\n          \"description\": \"Existing isolated code/design execution and judging policy.\",\n          \"path\": \"src/daemon/threads/review-worker-runtime.ts\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"preparation\",\n          \"label\": \"Shared preparation contract\",\n          \"description\": \"Proposed common lifecycle adapter around existing family validators; no replacement judge.\",\n          \"path\": \"src/workflow/review\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"source\",\n          \"label\": \"Verified source planning\",\n          \"description\": \"Existing ReviewSources/projection extended with bounded shared query sessions and batching.\",\n          \"path\": \"src/workflow/code-review/task-review/sources.ts\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"native\",\n          \"label\": \"Host native leases\",\n          \"description\": \"Existing intent-before-spawn, disposal and cancellation authority.\",\n          \"path\": \"src/daemon/threads/review-native-host.ts\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"history\",\n          \"label\": \"Full review history\",\n          \"description\": \"Existing project checkpoint writers at semantic input/result boundaries.\",\n          \"path\": \"src/workflow\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"context\",\n          \"label\": \"Immutable context bytes\",\n          \"description\": \"Stable verified source generation, separately versioned history bindings and retained query staging under aggregate capacity accounting. Includes digest-indexed staged packet descriptors and typed leaves; bounded writer and consumer windows, no eager inventory.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"lifecycle\",\n          \"label\": \"Publication / approval / cleanup\",\n          \"description\": \"Existing lifecycle gates consume the same qualified context and runtime proof.\",\n          \"path\": \"src/workflow\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"dependencies\": [\n        {\n          \"from\": \"surface\",\n          \"to\": \"host\",\n          \"label\": \"exact review control\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"from\": \"host\",\n          \"to\": \"runtime\",\n          \"label\": \"sole hot-state writer\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"from\": \"host\",\n          \"to\": \"worker\",\n          \"label\": \"dedicated owner / cancellation\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"from\": \"worker\",\n          \"to\": \"preparation\",\n          \"label\": \"acquire complete context\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"from\": \"preparation\",\n          \"to\": \"source\",\n          \"label\": \"qualify immutable evidence\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"from\": \"source\",\n          \"to\": \"native\",\n          \"label\": \"isolated bounded Git\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"from\": \"native\",\n          \"to\": \"runtime\",\n          \"label\": \"durable intent / closure\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"from\": \"preparation\",\n          \"to\": \"context\",\n          \"label\": \"write / read immutable generation\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"from\": \"preparation\",\n          \"to\": \"host\",\n          \"label\": \"private ready receipt / borrow\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"from\": \"worker\",\n          \"to\": \"history\",\n          \"label\": \"input and accepted feedback\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"from\": \"lifecycle\",\n          \"to\": \"preparation\",\n          \"label\": \"reuse or cold qualify once\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"from\": \"lifecycle\",\n          \"to\": \"runtime\",\n          \"label\": \"current resource / cancellation proof\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"from\": \"lifecycle\",\n          \"to\": \"history\",\n          \"label\": \"preserve before cleanup\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    \"adherence\": {\n      \"dimensions\": [\n        \"diagram-sequence\",\n        \"diagram-component\",\n        \"functional-coverage\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"companions\": [\n      {\n        \"kind\": \"diagram-mermaid\",\n        \"relPath\": \"docs/standalone/rework-review-preparation-context-lifecycle-end-E20261114470a1f61/S001/sequence-diagram.html\",\n        \"title\": \"Sequence diagram\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"kind\": \"diagram-mermaid\",\n        \"relPath\": \"docs/standalone/rework-review-preparation-context-lifecycle-end-E20261114470a1f61/S001/component-dependency.html\",\n        \"title\": \"Component dependencies\"\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"citations\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c1\",\n      \"kind\": \"code\",\n      \"ref\": \"src/workflow/code-review/task-review/admission.ts\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c2\",\n      \"kind\": \"code\",\n      \"ref\": \"src/daemon/threads/review-workers.ts\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c3\",\n      \"kind\": \"code\",\n      \"ref\": \"src/workflow/review/preparation-checkpoint.ts\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c4\",\n      \"kind\": \"step-output\",\n      \"ref\": \"s1.analyzeBundles[1]\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c5\",\n      \"kind\": \"prior-artifact\",\n      \"ref\": \".insr